The stairwell is cold and there is no elevator.
My suitcase is large and very heavy.
I slowly carry the suitcase up the stairs.
A woman comes quickly down the stairs.
She is friendly and has a small dog on a lead.
"Good evening!" she says.
"Good evening," I answer.
"Are you the new tenant?" she asks.
"Yes, I am the new tenant," I say.
"I am Sabine Krüger," the woman says.
"And this is my dog, Bruno."
"My name is Maya Flores," I say.
"Nice to meet you, Frau Krüger."
"Where are you from, Frau Flores?" she asks.
"I am from Mexico," I answer.
"Ah, from Mexico!"
"Welcome to Berlin!" she says.
"Thank you," I say.
Frau Krüger goes downstairs and I go upstairs.
